Load character cards at API startup

The /eavesdrop map could not finish a listen. startup_event() wired up every
subsystem — conversation manager, eavesdrop manager, dungeon master — but never
put anything in the NPC pool. conversation_manager then failed with
"NPC 'Thorne' not loaded" and POST /api/eavesdrop/listen answered 400.

The failure mode was nasty because everything before it worked: the map let you
walk to a spot, GET /check correctly answered "位置合适，可以听了。", and only the
final press of Listen failed. The endpoint path had never been exercised end to
end — the unit tests drive EavesdropManager directly and load cards themselves,
so they stayed green.

Loading the card glob at startup also means the API is usable the moment uvicorn
is up, with no /api/characters/load call first.

Add a regression test that closes the class of bug rather than this instance:
every NPC named in eavesdrop_spots.json must be obtainable from character_cards/.
TestContentWiring fails with the missing names if content and cards drift apart.

Tests: test_eavesdrop.py — 30 tests, all passing.
